#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:16
msgid "Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:19
msgid "Web Page Caching Bug Fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:21
msgid ""
":doc:`../general/caching` now caches the Response data after :ref:`after-"
"filters` are executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:22
msgid ""
"For example, if you enable :ref:`secureheaders`, the Response headers are"
" now sent when the page comes from the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:24
msgid ""
"If you have written **code based on this bug** that assumes changes to "
"the Response in \"after\" filters are not cached then **sensitive "
"information could be cached and compromised**. If this is the case, "
"change your code to disable caching of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:27
msgid "Others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:29
msgid ""
"The method ``Forge::createTable()`` no longer executes a ``CREATE TABLE "
"IF NOT EXISTS``.  When `$ifNotExists` is true, if the table is not found "
"in ``$db->tableExists($table)`` then ``CREATE TABLE`` is executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:30
msgid ""
"The second parameter ``$ifNotExists`` of ``Forge::_createTable()`` is "
"deprecated. It is no longer used and will be removed in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_422.rst:31
msgid ""
"When you use :php:func:`random_string()` with the first parameter "
"``'crypto'``, now if you set the second parameter ``$len`` to an odd "
"number, ``InvalidArgumentException`` will be thrown. Change the parameter"
" to an even number."
msgstr ""

